From 4b6f96598f17c3ababc157259c657c2fc86195a7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Roch=C3=A9=20Compaan?= <roche@upfrontsoftware.co.za>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 19:01:30 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 15/17] qwen35: decode Q4_K/Q6_K without re-deriving the header
 per element

The generic value<> path recomputes the super-block index, the 6-bit scale
unpacking and the nibble position for every element, so dense K-quant decode ran
at ~146 GB/s on a 3090, 16% of the card.

matvec_kquant gives each lane one 32-value sub-block: the header is decoded once,
the row is read in 128-byte spans, activations arrive as float4, and the token
loop reuses the dequantised values. Templated over T=1/2/4/8 and wired into the
decode dispatch for Q4_K (12) and Q6_K (14); the arithmetic is identical to
value<12>/value<14>, so the reference tests still define correctness.

Measured on the 27B Q4_K_M, residency on: 8.71 -> 15.05 t/s generation, prefill
unchanged at 126 t/s. test_qwen35_cuda_quant passes.

Also fix the margin override: an explicit DS4_CUDA_RESERVE_GIB was being clamped
up to the 6 GiB default floor, so the escape hatch could not lower the margin.
The floor now applies only to the default, and the post-copy revert check uses
the margin actually requested.
---
 ds4_cuda.cu        | 13 +++++---
 ds4_qwen4_cuda.cuh | 82 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 91 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

